% Problem 29. Chace vol. II pl. 51 (photograph XII, register 5), PDF pp. 149-150; Peet pp. 64-66 (Pl. J).
% The beginning of the problem is lost in copying: Chace fn 4 to No. 28: "The scribe has omitted the proof here and the statement of the next problem"; Peet: the copyist "has evidently missed out both the end of 28 and the beginning of 29"
No. 29
  1      10
  '4     2 '2
  '10    1
{Total 13 '2.}
  2/3    9              % 2/3 of 13 '2, the total above (not of 10)
"Total 22 '2."           % "dmd 22 '2" (black): 13 '2 and 9; quoted, since the notation's Total would add only the 9 after the last total
  '3     7 '2           % '3 of 22 '2
"Total 30."              % "dmd 30": 22 '2 and 7 '2; quoted for the same reason
  2/3    20             % 2/3 of 30
  '3     10             % '3 of 30
